h2. Steps to reproduce

* Create non terminal pages {{page:Sandbox/ABC}} and {{page:Sandbox/DEF}} with some content in each of them
* Include the latter into the former using the {{page}} parameter: {noformat}
{{include page="Sandbox/DEF"/}}
{noformat}

h2. Actual result

When viewing page {{Sandbox/ABC}} the content of {{Sandbox/DEF}} is correctly included, however the information tab displays "No included pages". Also, probably a side effect of the same bug: when editing the page, the included one is not shown in the document information panel. When using the {{include}} macro with the {{reference}} parameter instead, with reference {{Sandbox.DEF.WebHome}}, everything works as expected.

When including or displaying a page using the include or display macro, identical headings on the including and included page lead to duplicate ids.

*Steps to reproduce:*
 # Create a page A with content {{= Heading =}}
 # Create a page B with content
{code:java}
= Heading =
{{include reference="A"/}}
{code}

 # Save and view the page.

*Expected result:*

The two headings have different ids.

*Actual result:*

The two headings have the same id.

h2. Steps to reproduce

1. Create terminal page "Sandbox.A" with the following content:
{noformat}
[[Link to self>>doc:A||anchor="section1"]]
{noformat}

2. Rename "Sandbox.A" to "Sandbox.A.WebHome" with option "Update links" activated and without activating the redirects

h2. Expected result

The content of the page is udpated to the following:

{noformat}
[[Link to self>>doc:Sandbox.A.WebHome||anchor="section1"]]
{noformat}

or even better:
{noformat}
[[Link to self>>||anchor="section1"]]
{noformat}

h2. Actual result

The page contains the following link, which points at an inexistent page:

{noformat}
[[Link to self>>doc:Sandbox.A||anchor="section1"]]
{noformat}

When editing large pages (like the default Home page) and inserting text the server closes the connection.

The message from the server is:

{{1009 The decoded text message was too big for the output buffer and the endpoint does not support partial messages}}

