Note that {{org.webjars.npm:pagedjs}} WebJar cannot be installed or upgraded *directly* (explicitly) because it has some badly expressed dependencies (some development dependencies that shouldn't be listed). It needs to be installed / upgraded through the PDF Export Application which excludes those useless transitive dependencies, see https://github.com/xwiki/xwiki-platform/blob/xwiki-platform-15.1/xwiki-platform-core/xwiki-platform-export/xwiki-platform-export-pdf/xwiki-platform-export-pdf-ui/pom.xml#L124-L136 . But as [~vmassol] mentioned, the PDF Export Application is *already installed* (bundled) in XWiki 15.1, so you have it, no need to install anything.

{quote}
org.xwiki.component.manager.ComponentLookupException: Failed to lookup component [org.xwiki.export.pdf.script.PDFExportScriptService] identified by type [interface org.xwiki.script.service.ScriptService] and hint [export.pdf]
{quote}

You need to give us the *full* stack trace. But in any case, this doesn't seem related to the {{pagedjs}} WebJar which is a dependency of the PDF Export Application *UI* (wiki pages) not the *API* (Java code), and the script service is Java code, which doesn't depend nor use {{pagedjs}}. Pagedjs is used only in the PDF Export Sheet, which is a wiki page, part of the *UI* module.

Would be good to tell us exactly how we can reproduce your problem on a clean XWiki 15.1. Thanks.

