Follow these steps to reproduce:

* put this in a wiki page
{noformat}
{{documentTree finder="true" /}}
{noformat}
* save and then type something in the tree finder input, such as "test"
* hover one of the provided suggestions
* try to open the target wiki page in a separate browser tab -> it doesn't work because although the suggestion uses a link element under the hood, that link element doesn't have a proper URL set to target the corresponding wiki page

When performing a PDF export we get the following warning notification message:

{quote}
The PDF export log contains errors: null
{quote}

The PDF export works fine, but this message confuses the users, misleading them into thinking there is a problem, where in fact there's no error in the PDF export log.
